Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 08:37:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Alarm on silent turn-urgency observer outages

Why: failed or missing observations silently expired, so admission consumers could not distinguish unknown from empty. The observer has no alarm responsibility; gateway maintenance now detects enabled-host outages after an inclusive 600s grace, reuses one host repair card with hourly repeats and recovery comments. Named profiles and nondefault boards cannot duplicate the account alarm. No scoring or source access changes.

Proof: canonical focused suites: 100 passed (turn urgency, new alarm, existing worker-resource alarm); scripts/check --base origin/main green. New state tick-status tests and all state turn-urgency suites: 59 passed. Preliminary independent review edge cases covered: profile home, repeated recovery, cache/status crash, card/event crash, initial upgraded-board discovery. Live 11-minute incident proof remains required after both halves deploy.
